# Clean Code

Write code that is self-explanatory through good naming and structure. Prefer small, single-purpose functions with early-return guard clauses over deep nesting.

## Comments

Comments are the exception, not the rule. Well-named code needs none.

- Only comment to explain **why**: non-obvious intent, trade-offs, caveats, workarounds, or platform/library quirks.
- Never narrate **what** the code does or restate the code in prose.
- Never leave comments describing the change you just made (e.g. "added X", "now handles Y").
- When suppressing a linter rule, justify it inline (`// eslint-disable-next-line ... -- reason`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — narrates the obvious
// Increment the counter
counter += 1

// Loop over entries and filter logs
entries.filter((entry) => entry.endsWith('.log'))

// ✅ GOOD — explains a non-obvious reason
// Rollovers within the same millisecond would collide on the timestamp.
while (fs.existsSync(candidate)) { ... }

// Logging must never crash the app, so swallow any filesystem failure.
try { fs.appendFileSync(getActiveFilePath(), line) } catch {}
```

## Naming & Structure

- Descriptive verb-first function names (`resolveSelectedModel`, `createLogFilePath`, `getActiveFilePath`).
- `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for module-level constants (`MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES`, `MODEL_EXTENSION`).
- Extract private helpers at module scope; keep the exported/public surface obvious.
- Pass an options object (with a named `interface`) when a function takes several params.

## Types

- `interface` for object shapes (props, schemas, options); `type` for unions and aliases.
- Model variants as discriminated unions; use `as const` objects for enum-like maps.
- Let return types infer when obvious; annotate only when it adds clarity or safety.

## Error Handling

- Swallow-and-fallback for non-critical reads (return `[]`/`null`); rethrow user-facing `Error` messages for actionable failures.
- Normalize unknown errors with the shared `getErrorMessage` helper rather than assuming `.message`.

## React

- Function components only; name the props interface `<Component>Props`.
- Stabilize values passed down or into deps with `useCallback`/`useMemo`.
- Guard effect async work with an `isMounted` flag and clean up listeners on unmount.
- Context hooks (`useModel`) throw a clear error when used outside their provider.
- Compose class names with `clsx`; group related Tailwind classes across lines.

## Formatting

No semicolons, single quotes, 2-space indentation — matching the existing Prettier/ESLint setup.
